#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_advanced.rst:22
msgid "Adding a PHP event to your extension"
msgstr "Adding a PHP event to your extension"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_advanced.rst:23
msgid ""
"You can add PHP events to your own extension, allowing other extensions to "
"hook into parts of your extension to add functionality or modify its "
"behaviour. Basically, this involves you, the extension author, making your "
"own events at key points in the code of your extension that other extensions "
"can then listen for. If your extension is not enabled, the relevant code in "
"other extensions will be ignored. When your extension is enabled and the "
"event in question is called, the listeners in the other enabled extensions "
"will be run."
msgstr ""
"You can add PHP events to your own extension, allowing other extensions to "
"hook into parts of your extension to add functionality or modify its "
"behaviour. Basically, this involves you, the extension author, making your "
"own events at key points in the code of your extension that other extensions "
"can then listen for. If your extension is not enabled, the relevant code in "
"other extensions will be ignored. When your extension is enabled and the "
"event in question is called, the listeners in the other enabled extensions "
"will be run."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_advanced.rst:31
msgid "This is what an event looks like:"
msgstr "This is what an event looks like:"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_advanced.rst:47
msgid ""
"You will need to replace ``identifier`` with the name of your event. This "
"must be prefixed by your vendor and extension name and use only underscores "
"and lowercase letters for the prefix and name which have to be separated "
"with a dot."
msgstr ""
"You will need to replace ``identifier`` with the name of your event. This "
"must be prefixed by your vendor and extension name and use only underscores "
"and lowercase letters for the prefix and name which have to be separated "
"with a dot."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_advanced.rst:51
msgid ""
"Furthermore, ``var1`` and ``var2`` refer to the implied variables ``$var1`` "
"and ``$var2`` from the current scope. These are passed into the event and "
"are available through the $event array. They can be used and altered as "
"needed and then passed back from the event. When making a custom event, be "
"sure to provide as many variables from the event's scope as you can for "
"listeners to use."
msgstr ""
"Furthermore, ``var1`` and ``var2`` refer to the implied variables ``$var1`` "
"and ``$var2`` from the current scope. These are passed into the event and "
"are available through the $event array. They can be used and altered as "
"needed and then passed back from the event. When making a custom event, be "
"sure to provide as many variables from the event's scope as you can for "
"listeners to use."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_advanced.rst:58
msgid ""
"It is important once you create an event that is contained in a full release "
"that you do not change the event's identifier or otherwise alter the event "
"in such a way that breaks backwards compatibility unless absolutely "
"necessary. Otherwise, other extensions may break without warning! It is "
"probably best to publish a list of events provided by your extension and "
"make public note of any event changes prior to releasing a new version."
msgstr ""
"It is important once you create an event that is contained in a full release "
"that you do not change the event's identifier or otherwise alter the event "
"in such a way that breaks backwards compatibility unless absolutely "
"necessary. Otherwise, other extensions may break without warning! It is "
"probably best to publish a list of events provided by your extension and "
"make public note of any event changes prior to releasing a new version."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_advanced.rst:65
msgid ""
"If an event does not need any arguments, you can use this short version:"
msgstr ""
"If an event does not need any arguments, you can use this short version:"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_advanced.rst:72
msgid ""
"The ``$phpbb_dispatcher`` object is available from phpBB's dependency "
"injection container or as a global variable, so if you do not pass it as a "
"parameter to your method, use global ``$phpbb_dispatcher`` to make it "
"available."
msgstr ""
"The ``$phpbb_dispatcher`` object is available from phpBB's dependency "
"injection container or as a global variable, so if you do not pass it as a "
"parameter to your method, use global ``$phpbb_dispatcher`` to make it "
"available."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_advanced.rst:77
msgid "Adding a template event to your extension"
msgstr "Adding a template event to your extension"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_advanced.rst:78
msgid ""
"Besides PHP events there are also template events. Template events can be "
"used to extend the template of an extension, so other extensions can "
"manipulate the output of your extension. To create a template event you "
"simply add the EVENT tag to your template:"
msgstr ""
"Besides PHP events there are also template events. Template events can be "
"used to extend the template of an extension, so other extensions can "
"manipulate the output of your extension. To create a template event you "
"simply add the EVENT tag to your template:"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_advanced.rst:87
msgid ""
"The event can be used in the same way as the template events in the phpBB "
"Core. See :doc:`tutorial_events` on how to use these events."
msgstr ""
"The event can be used in the same way as the template events in the phpBB "
"Core. See :doc:`tutorial_events` on how to use these events."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_advanced.rst:90
msgid ""
"You must always prefix your event names with your vendor and extension name. "
"Make sure to only use underscores, numbers and lowercase letters."
msgstr ""
"You must always prefix your event names with your vendor and extension name. "
"Make sure to only use underscores, numbers and lowercase letters."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_advanced.rst:94
msgid ""
"Like with PHP events you should not change the identifier of the event after "
"a release of your extension. Other extensions might already be using your "
"event and would risk breaking."
msgstr ""
"Like with PHP events you should not change the identifier of the event after "
"a release of your extension. Other extensions might already be using your "
"event and would risk breaking."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_advanced.rst:99
msgid ""
"It is not recommended to reuse existing event names in different locations. "
"This should only be done if the code (nested HTML elements) around the event "
"is the same for both locations. Also think about other extensions: do they "
"always want to listen to both places, or just one? In case of doubt: use a "
"new and unique event."
msgstr ""
"It is not recommended to reuse existing event names in different locations. "
"This should only be done if the code (nested HTML elements) around the event "
"is the same for both locations. Also think about other extensions: do they "
"always want to listen to both places, or just one? In case of doubt: use a "
"new and unique event."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_advanced.rst:106
msgid "Using installation commands in ext.php"
msgstr "Using installation commands in ext.php"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_advanced.rst:107
msgid ""
"There are times when an extension may need to execute code while it is being "
"enabled, disabled or purged. Some examples may be to check that the board "
"meets the requirements of the extension, or to run some sort of set-up or "
"clean-up processes."
msgstr ""
"There are times when an extension may need to execute code while it is being "
"enabled, disabled or purged. Some examples may be to check that the board "
"meets the requirements of the extension, or to run some sort of set-up or "
"clean-up processes."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_advanced.rst:112
msgid ""
"This is done by adding a class to the root directory of an extension called "
"``ext.php``. It must extend ``\\phpbb\\extension\\base``. Extending the base "
"class permits custom code to be executed during the enabling, disabling or "
"purging of an extension with the following inherited methods:"
msgstr ""
"This is done by adding a class to the root directory of an extension called "
"``ext.php``. It must extend ``\\phpbb\\extension\\base``. Extending the base "
"class permits custom code to be executed during the enabling, disabling or "
"purging of an extension with the following inherited methods:"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_advanced.rst:117
msgid "``is_enableable()``"
msgstr "``is_enableable()``"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_advanced.rst:118
msgid "``enable_step()``"
msgstr "``enable_step()``"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_advanced.rst:119
msgid "``disable_step()``"
msgstr "``disable_step()``"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_advanced.rst:120
msgid "``purge_step()``"
msgstr "``purge_step()``"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_advanced.rst:122
msgid ""
"Suppose an extension wants to strictly requires phpBB 3.1.5 or later. We can "
"override the ``is_enableable()`` method, and use it to check phpBB's "
"version, and return a boolean result."
msgstr ""
"Suppose an extension wants to strictly requires phpBB 3.1.5 or later. We can "
"override the ``is_enableable()`` method, and use it to check phpBB's "
"version, and return a boolean result."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_advanced.rst:141
msgid ""
"If false is returned, the extension will not be installed and the user will "
"be notified their board does not meet the requirements of the extension. If "
"it returns true, installation will proceed."
msgstr ""
"If false is returned, the extension will not be installed and the user will "
"be notified their board does not meet the requirements of the extension. If "
"it returns true, installation will proceed."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_advanced.rst:145
msgid ""
"The ``ext.php`` class may contain any special installation commands in the "
"``enable_step()``, ``disable_step()`` and ``purge_step()`` methods. As it "
"is, these methods are defined in ``\\phpbb\\extension\\base``, which this "
"class extends, but you can overwrite them to give special instructions to "
"each step. For example:"
msgstr ""
"The ``ext.php`` class may contain any special installation commands in the "
"``enable_step()``, ``disable_step()`` and ``purge_step()`` methods. As it "
"is, these methods are defined in ``\\phpbb\\extension\\base``, which this "
"class extends, but you can overwrite them to give special instructions to "
"each step. For example:"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_advanced.rst:164
msgid ""
"Notice that we execute our code only if the incoming ``$old_state`` is "
"false. Once we have finished we must return an arbitrary value. Otherwise, "
"we simply return the state of the parent class."
msgstr ""
"Notice that we execute our code only if the incoming ``$old_state`` is "
"false. Once we have finished we must return an arbitrary value. Otherwise, "
"we simply return the state of the parent class."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_advanced.rst:168
msgid ""
"The phpBB `Board Rules <https://github.com/phpbb-extensions/boardrules/blob/"
"master/ext.php>`_ extension shows another example of this in order to "
"prepare the notifications system for the extension when enabling, disabling "
"and deleting the extension."
msgstr ""
"The phpBB `Board Rules <https://github.com/phpbb-extensions/boardrules/blob/"
"master/ext.php>`_ extension shows another example of this in order to "
"prepare the notifications system for the extension when enabling, disabling "
"and deleting the extension."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_advanced.rst:173
msgid ""
"The enable/disable/purge step methods allow for large processes to be paused "
"and resumed. If the returned value from the step method is not false, then "
"the returned value will be serialised and stored in the database. When the "
"step method is called again, the last known state will be de-serialised, and "
"it will continue to be executed until such time as false is returned."
msgstr ""
"The enable/disable/purge step methods allow for large processes to be paused "
"and resumed. If the returned value from the step method is not false, then "
"the returned value will be serialised and stored in the database. When the "
"step method is called again, the last known state will be de-serialised, and "
"it will continue to be executed until such time as false is returned."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_advanced.rst:180
msgid ""
"The serialised data is stored in the *phpbb_ext* table under the *ext_state* "
"field. Developers should never manipulate this field directly as the "
"serialisation is handled internally by phpBB."
msgstr ""
"The serialised data is stored in the *phpbb_ext* table under the *ext_state* "
"field. Developers should never manipulate this field directly as the "
"serialisation is handled internally by phpBB."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_advanced.rst:185
msgid "Using service collections"
msgstr "Using service collections"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_advanced.rst:186
msgid ""
"In 3.1, a new concept is that of \"services\". You can read up on exactly "
"what a service is `here <https://symfony.com/doc/current/book/"
"service_container.html>`_. The rest of this guide will assume you have basic "
"knowledge of services and how to use them. A service collection is basically "
"what it sounds like: a collection of services. Basically, when you define "
"your service, you give it a special \"tag\", which associates it with a "
"collection of services. Later on, this can be used to easily get a list of "
"services for use by your extension."
msgstr ""
"In 3.1, a new concept is that of \"services\". You can read up on exactly "
"what a service is `here <https://symfony.com/doc/current/book/"
"service_container.html>`_. The rest of this guide will assume you have basic "
"knowledge of services and how to use them. A service collection is basically "
"what it sounds like: a collection of services. Basically, when you define "
"your service, you give it a special \"tag\", which associates it with a "
"collection of services. Later on, this can be used to easily get a list of "
"services for use by your extension."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_advanced.rst:195
msgid ""
"To use this, you first create a service for your service collection. This "
"will actually point to a core phpBB object called "
"``phpbb\\di\\service_collection``."
msgstr ""
"To use this, you first create a service for your service collection. This "
"will actually point to a core phpBB object called "
"``phpbb\\di\\service_collection``."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_advanced.rst:207
msgid "Of course the service name and the tag name may be whatever you like."
msgstr "Of course the service name and the tag name may be whatever you like."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_advanced.rst:210
msgid ""
"To prevent duplicates in your tag you should use a unique tag name, "
"preferably in the form of vendor.extname.tag_name."
msgstr ""
"To prevent duplicates in your tag you should use a unique tag name, "
"preferably in the form of vendor.extname.tag_name."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_advanced.rst:213
msgid "Now, when you want to add a service to your collection, just tag it:"
msgstr "Now, when you want to add a service to your collection, just tag it:"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_advanced.rst:222
msgid ""
"Notice that the tag \"name\" value here corresponds to the tag \"tag\" value "
"in the previous service collection definition. Also, keep in mind that if "
"the class (in this case, ``thing_one``) extends another class, you will need "
"to provide the correct services and values for any parameters defined in the "
"constructor of the parent class, if necessary."
msgstr ""
"Notice that the tag \"name\" value here corresponds to the tag \"tag\" value "
"in the previous service collection definition. Also, keep in mind that if "
"the class (in this case, ``thing_one``) extends another class, you will need "
"to provide the correct services and values for any parameters defined in the "
"constructor of the parent class, if necessary."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_advanced.rst:228
msgid ""
"Finally, to use the collection of services, just pass the first service as "
"an argument to another service class. For instance, let's say I have a "
"manager object for my foobar extension and I want the manager to know about "
"all of the services in the \"foobar_collection\" service. When defining the "
"manager class, just give it the service collection as an argument."
msgstr ""
"Finally, to use the collection of services, just pass the first service as "
"an argument to another service class. For instance, let's say I have a "
"manager object for my foobar extension and I want the manager to know about "
"all of the services in the \"foobar_collection\" service. When defining the "
"manager class, just give it the service collection as an argument."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_advanced.rst:240
msgid ""
"That argument will return an instance of ``phpbb\\di\\service_collection``, "
"which extends ``ArrayObject`` so it can be used as an array containing the "
"service name of each item in the collection as the key, and an instance of "
"each of the service items as the corresponding value."
msgstr ""
"That argument will return an instance of ``phpbb\\di\\service_collection``, "
"which extends ``ArrayObject`` so it can be used as an array containing the "
"service name of each item in the collection as the key, and an instance of "
"each of the service items as the corresponding value."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_advanced.rst:245
msgid ""
"This system is used in the core for several features, including "
"notifications and authentication providers."
msgstr ""
"This system is used in the core for several features, including "
"notifications and authentication providers."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_advanced.rst:249
msgid "Ordered service collection"
msgstr "Ordered service collection"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_advanced.rst:251
msgid "Ordered service collections were introduced in phpBB 3.2."
msgstr "Ordered service collections were introduced in phpBB 3.2."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_advanced.rst:253
msgid ""
"Ordered service collections allow you to define the order in which services "
"are loaded, which is especially useful in cases where service priority and/"
"or dependency requires they be loaded in a specified order."
msgstr ""
"Ordered service collections allow you to define the order in which services "
"are loaded, which is especially useful in cases where service priority and/"
"or dependency requires they be loaded in a specified order."

